From 97ff5386dddd42dab70e82382a9301096aa558bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:32:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement XEP-0425 moderated message retraction in MUC rooms

Room moderators can retract any message in a room by its stanza ID with
`<moderate xmlns='urn:xmpp:message-moderate:1'>`. The room removes the
message from its history, broadcasts the retraction from its bare JID,
and runs the new `moderate_room_message` hook. mod_mam_muc_rdbms_arch
handles the hook by replacing the archived message with a tombstone that
keeps the moderator and the reason.

Add the `muc.moderateMessage` admin GraphQL command, which retracts a
message on behalf of the room, also in a persistent room that is not
running.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETaRHXo1LmPHqZB9SXMucM
