diff --git a/doc/modules/mod_mam.md b/doc/modules/mod_mam.md
index 5b1203d..138be2c 100644
--- a/doc/modules/mod_mam.md
+++ b/doc/modules/mod_mam.md
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@ The following criteria are used to find the original message:
 
 If more than one message matches the criteria, only the most recent one is retracted. To avoid this case, it is recommended to use a unique identifier (UUID) as the origin ID.
 
+#### Moderated retraction
+Messages retracted by room moderators with [XEP-0425: Moderated Message Retraction](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0425.html) are replaced in the room archive with a tombstone that keeps the moderator's occupant JID and the reason. See [`mod_muc`](mod_muc.md#message-moderation) for details. This also requires an RDBMS backend and the [`message_retraction`](#modulesmod_mammessage_retraction) option.
+
 #### Retraction on the stanza-id
 This module also implements an extension to the XEP, where it allows to specify the [`stanza-id`](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0359.html#stanza-id) as [created by](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0313.html#archives_id) the server's MAM, instead of the `origin-id` that the original [XEP-0424](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0424.html) specifies. It announces this capability under the namespace `urn:esl:message-retract-by-stanza-id:0`. This is specially useful in groupchats where the `stanza-id` of a message is shared and known for all participants.
 
diff --git a/doc/modules/mod_muc.md b/doc/modules/mod_muc.md
index c5f95ff..81743d3 100644
--- a/doc/modules/mod_muc.md
+++ b/doc/modules/mod_muc.md
@@ -7,6 +7,38 @@ It's a common XMPP group chat solution.
 This extension consists of two Erlang modules: `mod_muc` and `mod_muc_room`, the latter being the room code itself.
 Note that only `mod_muc` needs to be enabled in the configuration file.
 
+### Message moderation
+
+Rooms support [XEP-0425: Moderated Message Retraction](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0425.html) (`urn:xmpp:message-moderate:1`).
+An occupant with the `moderator` role can retract any message in the room by its [stanza ID](https://xmpp.org/extensions/xep-0359.html):
+
+```xml
+<iq type='set' to='room@muc.example.com' id='retract-1'>
+  <moderate id='stanza-id-1' xmlns='urn:xmpp:message-moderate:1'>
+    <retract xmlns='urn:xmpp:message-retract:1'/>
+    <reason>Spam</reason>
+  </moderate>
+</iq>
+```
+
+The room removes the message from its history and sends the retraction to all occupants from the room's bare JID:
+
+```xml
+<message type='groupchat' from='room@muc.example.com' id='...'>
+  <retract id='stanza-id-1' xmlns='urn:xmpp:message-retract:1'>
+    <moderated by='room@muc.example.com/moderator-nick' xmlns='urn:xmpp:message-moderate:1'/>
+    <reason>Spam</reason>
+  </retract>
+</message>
+```
+
+When [MUC archiving](mod_mam.md#enable-muc-message-archive) is enabled with the `rdbms` backend, the message is also replaced with a tombstone in the room archive.
+If the message is found neither in the archive nor in the room history, the request fails with `item-not-found`.
+Other occupants get a `forbidden` error.
+
+Administrators can do the same with the `muc.moderateMessage` command of the [GraphQL admin API](../graphql-api/Admin-GraphQL.md) (or `mongooseimctl muc moderateMessage`).
+In this case the moderator is the room itself.
+
